W006 got off to a good start. Dlvl 2 had a coaligned altar and the
entrance to the Mines. Dlvl 3 had a shop with speed boots and a leash.
Leash, speed boots, Magicbane, and a food ration. Time to try the
Mines.

I wear mithril plate because my spellcasting is nothing great yet
anyway. A coaligned priest in Minetown! That alone is almost as good
as getting a wish. A housecat named Fang can kill guards; one was
carrying a +3 small shield, another has +2 gloves.

Most of all, I buy a magic lamp, to go along with the one I already
picked up un the way down. Neither one is blessed. I dilute 3
unidentified potions and pray. On my first rub, I get +2 SDSM. Lovely.

On the way down to the luckstone, I find another magic lamp and a
polymorph trap and a magic whistle. My pet red dragon and I proceed
down and find the Gnome King's Wine Cellar! That's almost worth a wish
by itself, because of the several uncursed booze that can easily be
diluted. In fact, I break a fountain, drop most of my stuff, and jump
in the pool carrying booze. Now I have a decent supply of holy water,
and two magic lamps.

Another wish? Why not try, but what to wish for? Gotta be an artifact
-- a second early wish, only one artifact (MagicBane) exists yet,
these are the perfect conditions for artifact-fishing. Bad choice, I
go for PYEC, figuring I can ditch the CoMR and still have two sources
of MR. I thought I had just read somewhere that PYEC also helps
against random cursing.

Exploring carefully on the way back up, I find a BoH. This makes it a
lot easier to carry the broad pick I've been using to dig with.

Did I mention that I started with the spell of extra healing? I don't
think Fang could have beaten up the shopkeepers without its help.
After buying protection, I take stock. Basically, I've got 90% of an
AK, and it's early in the game.

Back to the main dungeon, and wander on down. I spent a long time
descending, using some wands of create monster by the altar on Dlvl 6
(I got Cleaver by accident; I got a spellbook or two (including the
all-important identify) by praying; I got crowned, which gave me some
nice resistances), doing a level or 2 of Sokoban (I dislike sokoban),
finding a +2 oilskin cloak, finding very few other useful things.

Fang got turned into a leocrotta somewhere near the Medusa level; we
walked back all the way to the polytrap in the Mines to make Fang into
a red ampersand. I bought more protection.

On the Medusa level. No way to levitate except for one potion. No
blindfold.
Interesting. Boring to go back again and find the one blindfold I
remember seeing somewhere; can't do the Quest, need more experience.
What to do?

I dig down, find the stairs, quaff a potion of blindness, go up, and
apply a mirror! How sweet it is!

This feels good.

AFtermath:
I couldn't get back up yet, at least not without wearing the cursed -2
boots of levity. But, as it turned out, the Castle was no problem at
all for me, although Fang did not survive. In fact, I went up from
level 12 to 13 by fighting! And I got hold of a potion of +level, and
the junk in the Castle included a T-shirt and dextrous gloves, leaving
me free to wish for a marker and a Helm of Brill.

Waste a wish on =oL? Never! I uncurse the flying boots and go back to
do the Quest.

Waste a wish on =oL? Never! It's off to find the vibrating square.

There's nothing worse than a cowardly major demon with a wand of
digging. I had a running pursuit that covered three demon-lair levels
and I got my brain sucked by a summoned nasty before I polished off
the three biggies and the two they summoned. (Note to self: those
levels were never properly checked for objects of interest).

I ran into an Archon in Vlad's tower. Cast "tame" half a dozen times,
and succeeded; immediately genocided w and t, breaking another
conduct. Also tamed and named a silver dragon, and tamed a nameless
warg.

Waste a wish on =oL? Never! This is a great excuse to break one more
conduct.
By polymorphing rings and things I get a can of grease, plus rings of
levitation and polycontrol. With polycontrol, I can break more
conduct, and proudly conduct a conduct-free ascension!

And now I'm back on Dlvl 6, sacrificing and summoning. There is
nothing left to do except waking up Rodney, but too many important
spells will wear out too soon. I have to spend a few thousand turns
just waiting for spells to be unlearned so I can relearn them. Oh,
well, maybe I can get an oilskin sack.
Or a saddle; I could go back and retame Silver, who I abandoned
somewhere.
And I really must polyself and lay some stoning grenades.

Archie, my pet Archon, is of course still with me.

